@startuml state-issue-lifecycle
title CityFix — Issue Lifecycle
skinparam shadowing false

state "Reported" as Reported
state "Verified" as Verified
state "Rejected" as Rejected
state "Duplicate" as Duplicate
state "Assigned" as Assigned
state "In Repair" as InRepair
state "Resolved" as Resolved

[*] --> Reported : citizen submits report [category and location given] (F-003)

Reported --> Verified : administrator verifies (F-009)
Reported --> Rejected : administrator rejects [reason entered] (F-009)
Reported --> Duplicate : administrator marks duplicate\n[existing report selected] (F-009)

Verified --> Assigned : administrator assigns worker\n[priority, deadline set;\nworker is from responsible department] (F-010)

Assigned --> InRepair : worker starts repair (F-012)
Assigned --> Resolved : worker marks resolved\n[after photo uploaded] (F-012, F-013)
InRepair --> Resolved : worker marks resolved\n[after photo uploaded] (F-012, F-013)

Assigned --> Verified : worker returns issue\n[explanation entered] (F-014)
InRepair --> Verified : worker returns issue\n[explanation entered] (F-014)

Assigned : priority raised and administrator alerted\nwhen deadline approaches without updates (F-017)

Rejected --> [*]
Duplicate --> [*]
Resolved --> [*]

note bottom of Resolved
  Every status change is saved in the status history
  and creates an in-app notification for the citizen (F-008).
end note
@enduml
